# --- build output ---------------------------------------------------------
# `dist/` holds the released binary and `dist_<ver>/` the candidate for the
# version being built; neither belongs in git.  A 37 MB one-file EXE would make
# every clone heavy, and because git keeps every blob forever, each future
# version would add another 37 MB to the history.  Releases are attached to a
# GitHub Release instead -- see the README.
dist/
dist_*/
build/
build_*/

# --- python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.env

# --- tooling --------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor/agent scratch space: memory logs and per-session state, not sources.
.workbuddy/
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- generated pages ------------------------------------------------------
# `visualization/deck_tree.py` writes one ~3 MB HTML per mod.  It is an output,
# reproducible with one command, so it does not belong in the history.
编制结构-*.html
organization-chart-*.html

# --- internal recon -------------------------------------------------------
# Reconnaissance reports quote one specific mod's organisation, unit counts
# and naming quirks.  They are development notes for this editor, not
# documentation for whoever installs it, so they stay local.  `doc/使用教程.md`
# is the manual and *is* shipped -- the pattern stays deliberately narrow.
doc/*勘查报告.md
# Handover briefs for other projects: game-format facts plus one specific
# mod's figures, same reasoning as the recon reports above — local only.
doc/移交*.md
